    "durationMs": 151338,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested. `sh start.sh` applies Alembic migrations and serves on 0.0.0.0:8000.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app (SQLAlchemy 2.0 declarative models, psycopg3 engine rewritten from `DATABASE_URL`, pydantic-settings config, no hard-coded credentials)\n- `migrations/` — Alembic setup reading `DATABASE_URL`, with an initial `links` table migration (unique indexed `code`, `Text` url, `clicks`)\n- `start.sh`, `requirements.txt`, `README.md` (includes the start-the-server section), plus a 29-test pytest suite\n\n**Requirement handling worth noting:**\n- URLs are validated permissively (scheme `http`/`https` + host present, control chars rejected) and stored/echoed **unchanged** — no pydantic URL normalization\n- Codes match `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$` on POST bodies and path params; invalid format → 422, unknown code → 404, duplicate custom code → 409 (unique constraint + race-safe retry for generated codes)\n- All error responses (404/409/422, including malformed JSON via a custom `RequestValidationError` handler) return JSON with an `error` field\n- `/r/{code}` does an atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` and 302-redirects with `Location` set to the stored URL\n\n**Verified end-to-end:** all 29 tests pass against the live server; created a link with 2 clicks, killed the server, restarted via `start.sh` — clicks and data survived, and re-running migrations is a no-op. The database was truncated afterward, so the automated suite starts clean."
